Z||000012||sqoach||09-26-2001||08:05 PM||||Wow! Nice interiors guys! Man, I've got a lot of work ahead of me. Question for the people that did the armrests and center console black. Do you have problems with it rubbing off? Did you use vinyl paint? Dye? Have any tips? I'll be doing my interior in black and dark grey.<P>William, nice steering wheel. I've got one just like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">           <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Joe Torma||09-26-2001||09:00 PM||||Damn...those all black dash and consoles look great!||||reg||1
Z||000014||California Kid||09-26-2001||09:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR>[B]Question for the people that did the armrests and center console black. Do you have problems with it rubbing off? Did you use vinyl paint? Dye? Have any tips? I'll be doing my interior in black and dark grey.<BR>]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Mine has been done for 3 years now with no indications of wear showing. Make sure you use a good interior paint (auto painters supply store), and all parts must be cleaned to remove all traces of armoral/wax, etc. You should do a alcohol wipe prior to paint. One trick I did, was to paint dash while it was still in the car. Covered everything (not painted) with very thin plastic drop cloth and masking tap (very easy to work with. On the inside of the windshield, I used a spray bottle with water and few drops of dish soap. Sprayed windshield and put news paper against it, stays in place for a long time (just don't let it dry there, remove as soon as paint is tacked up).<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||kempo||09-26-2001||09:52 PM||||Hey FieroMaster88- what do your extra gauges on the pillar monitor?  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroMaster88||09-26-2001||09:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kempo:<BR><B>Hey FieroMaster88- what do your extra gauges on the pillar monitor?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>At the moment one is Voltage and the other is the Air Fuel ratio.  Soon i am gonna put the aux gauge cluster in and put the oil pressure and voltage auto meter gauges in there...and put a boost/vac gauge in place of the voltemeter on the pillar.<BR>||||reg||1
